Instead I want to focus on the new footage in this trailer which parodies many familiar

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:36.880
Sci-Fi and Fantasy properties that we all know and love

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:39.860
and try to predict some of the satirical stories they might have planned.

00:01:39.860 --> 00:01:42.779
Let's start off with pickle Rick.
Which for fans should be a familiar image.

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:45.700
We saw a short animatic from this episode at Comic Con last year,

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:50.060
which we see part of again here in a more finished form, and it looks fantastic!

00:01:50.070 --> 00:01:52.940
We also get to see how Rick escapes this septic hellhole as he explodes

00:01:52.940 --> 00:01:56.840
out of a toilet wearing a makeshift gas mask made out of a rat's head.

00:01:56.840 --> 00:02:00.320
Later it seems he finds himself being chased by some armed agent-type goons,

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:04.780
And he later gets a drop on them by messaging an explosive code that sets off an insanely

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:07.620
huge bomb hidden under the desk they're staring at.

00:02:07.620 --> 00:02:11.000
And I'm guessing this might be a reference to Independence Day ,making fun of

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:15.100
the ridiculous idea of being able to send a computer virus to aliens.

00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:18.760
Also, that's a pretty complex bomb to have just built

00:02:18.760 --> 00:02:21.140
when you're the size of a shriveled up cucumber.

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:24.100
So I'm wondering, is this another one
of Rick's circuitous plans?

00:02:24.100 --> 00:02:25.920
Also, how did he end up in the sewer?

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:29.470
And if this isn't his plan, 
why was he so excited to be a pickle?

00:02:29.470 --> 00:02:34.460
I mean between having to construct an entire Rube Goldberg iron rat suit device with your tongue,,

00:02:34.460 --> 00:02:37.500
And be chased by firearm-wielding ruffians,

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:40.390
I don't imagine Rick is enjoying himself all that much.

00:02:40.390 --> 00:02:41.880
I don't know, you let me know what you think.

00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:45.180
Okay the next storyline I noticed seems to 
be a mixture of Avatar and Tomorrowland

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:47.400
as Rick flies with Jerry in his ship towards this

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:50.360
biodome city in the middle of this Pandora-like planet.

00:02:50.360 --> 00:02:55.860
Things naturally seem to take a turn for the worst as Rick and Jerry find themselves in a roller coaster ride

00:02:55.860 --> 00:02:59.680
that has two unfriendly looking aliens trying to kill Rick behind them.

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:02.040
It's a missable moment, but if you look closely in this shot,

00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:04.580
you can see one of them holding a rifle at Rick's head.

00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:07.509
Of course things get worse when the roller coaster crashes outside the park and

00:03:07.509 --> 00:03:10.460
Jerry finds himself alone in the path of this Alien beast,

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:14.380
reminiscent of a moment from Avatar, when Jake Sully runs into a similar situation.

00:03:14.380 --> 00:03:17.240
Now there's another very missable thing here,

00:03:17.260 --> 00:03:20.320
I've heard some people notice and it's this hole in the middle of Rick's shirt.

00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:23.709
Some people think this has to be a connection to an Iron Man-like scenario,

00:03:23.709 --> 00:03:26.880
But I'm pretty sure that's blood surrounding that hole.

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:31.980
So it almost seems like at some point, Rick got shot
and either the wound healed,

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:34.700
or maybe he was wearing some sort of protective layer underneath.

00:03:34.700 --> 00:03:38.660
Either way it connects to another clue as to what might be happening this episode,

00:03:38.660 --> 00:03:41.680
as we later see the same Rick with 
the same hole in his shirt

00:03:41.680 --> 00:03:45.400
reveal himself to be a robot with 
a Transformer-like laser arm.

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:48.420
So I'm thinking this wasn't even our original C-137 Rick.

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:52.020
After all, the first episode of the season we see Rick get Jerry kicked out

00:03:52.020 --> 00:03:54.080
of the house and seem very happy about it.

00:03:54.080 --> 00:03:55.140
So which Rick is this?

00:03:55.140 --> 00:03:56.920
And actually, is this our original Jerry?

00:03:56.920 --> 00:04:00.860
After all, we saw in Mortynight Run there are various Jerry's that all the Rick's are aware of.

00:04:00.860 --> 00:04:02.000
Okay, let's move on to the next episode.

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:04.920
This is clearly a Mad Max homage from start to finish.

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:10.080
We have the motorcade, there's an Immortan Joe-like character being killed by Summer in a Furiosa role,

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:13.460
using a shotgun that looks madly similar to Max's.

00:04:13.460 --> 00:04:15.920
At first I thought this might be in the Cronenberg world

00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:18.939
as I tried desperately to figure out what
they were cooking on that skewer,

00:04:18.940 --> 00:04:22.680
but then I remembered that the serum Rick made in Rick Potion #9

00:04:22.680 --> 00:04:26.300
only affects people that are not related to Morty and himself.

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:29.600
So unless everyone in this shot is related, I think it's safe

00:04:29.600 --> 00:04:32.300
to assume that this is a place we haven't visited yet.

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:36.400
Also, If you look closely at Rick at the front of the motorcade, you'll notice this gun is holding

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:40.060
is the same gun he is holding when he, Morty and Summer fall out of a portal

00:04:40.060 --> 00:04:43.180
in the garage, as if they just narrowly missed some sort of dark demise.

00:04:43.180 --> 00:04:47.410
So I'm thinking things are going to work out from this time around, but what I'm really curious about, is

00:04:47.410 --> 00:04:50.290
what is this green glowing object next to Rick in the passenger seat?

00:04:50.290 --> 00:04:53.280
I don't see Morty anywhere, but I
also don't think that this is him.

00:04:53.280 --> 00:04:57.099
More likely it's something that Rick's going to use either to save Morty or trade for Morty's life

00:04:57.100 --> 00:05:00.280
Or it might just be a totally different character entirely.

00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:04.040
Moving on to another episode, we get a very brief glimpse of is the Vindicators,

00:05:04.040 --> 00:05:07.400
a Guardians of Galaxy/Avengers like group of superheroes

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:09.100
that seem to enroll Morty as part of the group.

00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:14.380
If you close in the insignia on Morty's jacket, it matches the same insignia on Chris Pratt's looking character,

00:05:14.380 --> 00:05:19.940
and the Insignia on the base, the pulsating purple gem that indicates to Rick when they need him.

00:05:19.940 --> 00:05:23.439
Gems, cosmic superheroes, a hellish landscape with a giant overlord?

00:05:23.440 --> 00:05:27.240
I think this is going to be a very heavy parody of the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

