Now there was one last storyline I was able to hone in on, but before I talk about that,

00:06:46.500 --> 00:06:48.620
let me just acknowledge the scenes I couldn't connect to anything.

00:06:48.620 --> 00:06:51.460
There's a shot of Morty and Beth blowing up Summer to the size of the Iron Giant,

00:06:51.460 --> 00:06:55.380
which ends up being a double reference to Honey I Blew Up The Kid, and The 50ft Woman.

00:06:55.380 --> 00:06:58.480
And it's also followed by the introduction of a new character, Jean!

00:06:58.480 --> 00:07:00.600
Who is obviously inspired by Wilson,

00:07:00.600 --> 00:07:04.520
the friendly neighbor from one of my favorite shows as a 90s kid, Home Improvement.

00:07:04.520 --> 00:07:08.580
We also see an emotionless Morty with an arm the size of the Hulk's

00:07:08.580 --> 00:07:12.540
choking out this poor guy in a bathtub before being interrupted by Rick,

00:07:12.540 --> 00:07:16.020
mixing potions or possibly alcohol in the corner.

00:07:16.020 --> 00:07:17.900
Now this could be a Game of Thrones style episode,

00:07:17.900 --> 00:07:21.240
but people have also brought up The Witcher, and I'm apt to agree because

00:07:21.240 --> 00:07:25.360
both Dan Harmon and Justin Roiland have spoken very fondly of that video game series.

00:07:25.360 --> 00:07:28.720
There is this quick scene of Rick and Morty tied to a giant piano device,

00:07:28.720 --> 00:07:31.400
in the Most Adam West's Batman scenario I've ever seen.

00:07:31.400 --> 00:07:34.360
I mean look how deliciously camp this all is.

00:07:34.360 --> 00:07:37.329
There's a giant piano with an even 
smaller piano on top of it,

00:07:37.330 --> 00:07:41.949
and I'm willing to bet a lunch that that piano is directly connected the hammers above our heroes' heads.

00:07:41.949 --> 00:07:45.040
There's a part of me that thinks this could also be connected to the Vindicators episode,

00:07:45.040 --> 00:07:48.500
because the color scheme of this place matches the scene I mentioned earlier,

00:07:48.500 --> 00:07:53.380
but these dead characters all look exactly the same, and Morty isn't wearing his Vindicator jacket.

00:07:53.380 --> 00:07:57.309
But then again, this could be moments before the Vindicators come in and save the two of them.

00:07:57.310 --> 00:08:01.000
And there's this final shot of Summer with a more beefed-up, cyber version of herself

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:03.159
getting ready to possibly murder Rick?

00:08:03.159 --> 00:08:06.280
I don't know, this whole shot leaves a lot to the imagination.

00:08:06.280 --> 00:08:10.500
Some people have even guessed this might be the original Summer from Cronenberg World,

00:08:10.509 --> 00:08:13.380
but I think it's kind of lucky considering how much she and her parents

00:08:13.380 --> 00:08:15.279
were against Rick's technology in the last episode.

00:08:15.280 --> 00:08:19.839
But then again, maybe she's decided to embrace this evil to destroy the evil that created it.

00:08:19.840 --> 00:08:21.880
I don't know. I'm not an expert in this stuff after all,

00:08:21.880 --> 00:08:24.540
I'm literally just guessing off of like, 30 frames of footage.

00:08:24.540 --> 00:08:27.820
Okay, so there's another episode I've been skirting around, and it's possibly

00:08:27.820 --> 00:08:29.680
the most interesting storyline that's been revealed.

00:08:29.680 --> 00:08:32.080
And that's involving the Melted Morty and Rick.

00:08:32.080 --> 00:08:35.740
Now throughout the entire trailer, there's
 these two green boogie men

00:08:35.740 --> 00:08:38.520
that are seen battling Rick and 
Morty in the normal world,

00:08:38.520 --> 00:08:40.700
leading us to believe that these 
are the villains of this episode.

00:08:40.700 --> 00:08:46.160
But this final scene turns everything upside down as we realize that Rick and Morty, seemingly covered in the

00:08:46.160 --> 00:08:50.760
goo they're standing in, their faces melting, are trying to escape this putrid, melty-face hell.

00:08:50.760 --> 00:08:52.840
By the way there are a lot of hellscapes in this trailer.

00:08:52.840 --> 00:08:54.960
A desert, a sewer, a literal hell,

00:08:54.960 --> 00:08:57.240
and now this green, snot-rot location.

00:08:57.240 --> 00:09:00.320
Rick was not kidding when they said this is going to their darkest year ever.

00:09:00.320 --> 00:09:04.380
Anyway I get off track. People seem to think that this location is also the Cronenberg world,

00:09:04.380 --> 00:09:09.100
but I beg to differ because the aliens we see all look like they originated from different species,

00:09:09.100 --> 00:09:13.320
and all the surroundings seem more like the creatures have melted rather than transformed.

00:09:13.320 --> 00:09:16.900
Still, wherever this is, Rick and Morty seem to have been put here by someone.

00:09:16.900 --> 00:09:20.360
And another theory is that these two non-green Rick and Morty's could be the evil Rick and Morty

00:09:20.360 --> 00:09:22.520
from Season one's Close Rick-Counters of the Rick Kind.

00:09:22.520 --> 00:09:26.900
Now, granted that Rick was a robot, but we never did see where the Morty that was controlling him went.

00:09:26.900 --> 00:09:29.789
This could be him, and this Rick could be a robot Rick.

00:09:29.790 --> 00:09:35.060
Or this could also just be a regular Rick and Morty so desperate to find a safe place to call their own.

00:09:35.060 --> 00:09:39.869
One of the most interesting things about this show has always been the amorality of a lot of Rick's decisions.

00:09:39.870 --> 00:09:43.780
Yeah sure, some of the Rick's we meet are jerks, but most of them are just like Rick -

00:09:43.780 --> 00:09:45.860
Jerks. But you know, lovable jerks.

00:09:45.860 --> 00:09:47.940
Since the first season I've always wondered what would happen if we started

00:09:47.940 --> 00:09:49.540
following another pair of Rick and Morty.

00:09:49.540 --> 00:09:51.760
Sometimes I wasn't even sure we were still following the same one.

00:09:51.760 --> 00:09:53.180
And this could be that story.

00:09:53.180 --> 00:09:54.380
So, where do you think they are?

00:09:54.390 --> 00:09:57.220
Is this a Cronenberg world? And are these our original Rick and Morty?

00:09:57.220 --> 00:09:59.560
Or are these just another pair of Rick and Morty's trying to survive?

